    "message": "Guidelines note that in patients on TDF admitted to hospital, intercurrent illnesses with dehydration or sepsis may cause deterioration in renal function. Patient has severe gastroenteritis with 5 days of vomiting and diarrhoea, hypotension (90/60), tachycardia, and two affected family members, indicating infective gastroenteritis. The high urea-to-creatinine ratio (24:1) and absence of proteinuria favour pre-renal AKI from volume depletion rather than TDF nephrotoxicity. Creatinine was normal (0.9) until this acute illness. Guidelines recommend switching to ABC+3TC+DTG only when renal impairment develops due to TDF; this AKI has a clear alternative cause. Permanent TDF discontinuation may therefore be unnecessary if renal function recovers with rehydration.",
